== Fifth generation (W213; 2016) ==
{{main|Mercedes-Benz E-Class (W213)}}

[[File:Mercedes-AMG E 53 (W213) FL IMG 3965.jpg|thumb|Mercedes-AMG E53 (W213 facelift)]]
The fifth generation E-Class was unveiled at the 2016 [[North American International Auto Show]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.worldcarfans.com/115051193606/next-generation-mercedes-benz-e-class-sedan-will-likely |title=Next generation Mercedes-Benz E-Class Sedan will likely debut in January 2016 at NAIAS [spy video] |work=Motor1.com |access-date=2015-05-12 |archive-date=2015-05-13 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150513194251/http://www.worldcarfans.com/115051193606/next-generation-mercedes-benz-e-class-sedan-will-likely |url-status=live }}</ref> This generation E-Class has design cues from the larger [[Mercedes-Benz S-Class (W222)|W222 S-Class]] and the smaller [[Mercedes-Benz C-Class (W205)|W205 C-Class]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.autoevolution.com/news/2016-mercedes-e-class-w213-first-interior-spy-photos-s-class-inspiration-89573.html# |title=2016 Mercedes E-Class (W213) First Interior Spy Photos: S-CLass Inspiration |author=Mihnea Radu |work=autoevolution |date=3 December 2014 |access-date=2014-12-23 |archive-date=2014-12-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141223214649/http://www.autoevolution.com/news/2016-mercedes-e-class-w213-first-interior-spy-photos-s-class-inspiration-89573.html |url-status=live }}</ref> While the W212 E-Class has tighter surface and harder edges, the new model is curvier and more flowing.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://indianautosblog.com/2015/05/2016-mercedes-e-class-naias-2016-178443#ixzz3ZsnOcVNY |title=2016 Mercedes E Class to world debut at NAIAS 2016 |date=11 May 2015 |access-date=2015-05-12 |archive-date=2015-05-12 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150512163851/http://indianautosblog.com/2015/05/2016-mercedes-e-class-naias-2016-178443#ixzz3ZsnOcVNY |url-status=live }}</ref>

Engine options for the W213 E-Class saw a major update, switching back to inline six-cylinder engines from the previous V6 engines,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.carmagazine.co.uk/spy-shots/mercedes-benz/mercedes-e-class-2016-spied-straight-sixes-are-back/ |title=Mercedes E-class (2016) spied: straight sixes are back! |work=CAR Magazine |access-date=2015-04-22 |archive-date=2015-04-22 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20150422175722/http://www.carmagazine.co.uk/spy-shots/mercedes-benz/mercedes-e-class-2016-spied-straight-sixes-are-back/ |url-status=live }}</ref> along with a new generation of four-cylinder diesel engines, codenamed [[Mercedes-Benz OM654 engine|OM654]], while retaining existing four-cylinder petrol engines.<ref name="2016eclassautocar">{{cite web |url=http://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/new-cars/2016-mercedes-benz-e-class-spotted-engines-and-launch-date |title=2016 Mercedes-Benz E-Class - engines and launch date |first=Greg | last = Kable |work=Autocar |access-date=2015-10-16 |archive-date=2015-07-26 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20150726151952/http://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/new-cars/2016-mercedes-benz-e-class-spotted-engines-and-launch-date |url-status=live }}</ref>

The W213 E-Class is the second-most technologically advanced Mercedes after the new [[Mercedes-Benz S-Class|S-Class]].{{According to whom|date=September 2026}} The E-Class received the latest in autonomous driving technology for use at highway speeds, capable of piloting itself up to speeds of {{convert|130|mph|km/h|abbr=on}} for up to 2 minutes. The system uses a complex array of motion sensors, radars, and cameras to scan the road ahead, and requires the driver's hands to be placed on the wheel at all times.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://performancedrive.com.au/2016-mercedes-e-class-will-be-capable-of-autonomous-driving-1020/ |title=2016 Mercedes E-Class will be capable of autonomous driving |work=PerformanceDrive |date=10 June 2015 |access-date=2015-06-29 |archive-date=2015-06-15 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150615011411/http://performancedrive.com.au/2016-mercedes-e-class-will-be-capable-of-autonomous-driving-1020/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.worldcarfans.com/115042292626/mercedes-benz-says-autonomous-technology-is-imminent |title=Mercedes-Benz says autonomous technology is imminent, could debut on 2016 E-Class |work=Worldcarfans |access-date=2015-04-22 |archive-date=2015-04-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150423130327/http://www.worldcarfans.com/115042292626/mercedes-benz-says-autonomous-technology-is-imminent |url-status=live }}</ref> This feature was also available on the fourth-generation Mercedes-AMG E 63 model.

In 2020, Mercedes-Benz introduced a facelift to the W213.{{clear}}

== Sixth generation (W214; 2023) ==
[[File:Mercedes-Benz E 200 d AMG Line (W 214) – f 05072025.jpg|thumb|Mercedes-Benz E 200d (W214)]]
{{main|Mercedes-Benz E-Class (W214)}}

The sixth generation E-Class debuted on April 25, 2023. Body styles include the saloon and estate (wagon), while coupés and convertibles were discontinued. As part of a consolidation of model ranges, executive coupés and convertibles will slot between the E-Class and C-Class in size under the new [[Mercedes-Benz CLE|CLE]] nameplate.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2024 Mercedes-Benz E-Class teased ahead of April 25 debut |url=https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1139285_2024-mercedes-benz-e-class-teased-ahead-of-april-25-debut |access-date=2023-04-11 |website=Motor Authority |date=6 April 2023 |language=en |archive-date=2023-04-10 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230410211424/https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1139285_2024-mercedes-benz-e-class-teased-ahead-of-april-25-debut |url-status=live }}</ref>

